{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"df0d7e8582b9e1f9","name":"card_event_code_of_bushido","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Base/events/card_event_code_of_bushido","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CODE OF BUSHIDO","text":"Choose and discard an air unit to destroy a unit with 5 or less attack.","flavorText":"Bushido means \"the way of the warrior\" and is a Japanese term for the codes of honor and ideals that dictate the samurai way of life. The code is typified by 8 virtues: Righteousness and justice, heroic courage, benevolence and compassion, respect, honesty and sincerity, honor, duty and loyalty, self-control. These all seem like righteous codes and a roadmap to good living and happiness. However, perverse theories of Bushido dominated Japanese intellectual life and military command from 1930-45, which seemed to fuel Japan’s determination to fight to the very last man and woman and many link it to the atrocities committed by their soldiers during WWII.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_code_of_bushido","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_code_of_bushido_title","SourceString":"CODE OF BUSHIDO","LocalizedString":"CODE OF BUSHIDO"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_code_of_bushido_text","SourceString":"Choose and discard an air unit to destroy a unit with 5 or less attack.","LocalizedString":"Choose and discard an air unit to destroy a unit with 5 or less attack."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_code_of_bushido_history","SourceString":"Bushido means \"the way of the warrior\" and is a Japanese term for the codes of honor and ideals that dictate the samurai way of life. The code is typified by 8 virtues: Righteousness and justice, heroic courage, benevolence and compassion, respect, hones